{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Verify issue-resolution #877, #878, and #879 fixes against reported defects and pinned contracts","packet_sha256":"d8b6309ca8386d1b0abcfa409d8b626293c832d62482e330b543f27fe857b8c8","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"1eeb8a99496a75e9ce4d5df70123eecd303bf77b07e1d27826608ea090423fce","verdict":"pass","target_observations":[{"target":"#877","verdict":"pass","summary":"The abnormal-lane checkpoint handles merge state before the empty-change skip, commits a fully resolved in-scope merge without a pathspec, and reports unresolved or mixed-scope merges as distinct blockers. A clean lane tree with commits beyond base reuses its tip SHA. The task-run call passes a committed checkpoint SHA as target_head; completion uses target_head or observed HEAD for scope evidence, then records the resulting observed head as target_sha.","evidence":["task_run_checkpoint.py calls _merge_state first; conflicted paths raise UnresolvedMergeError, and resolved merge dirty paths outside refreshed scopes raise MixedScopeMergeError.","task_run_git.py checks unmerged index paths and both staged and unstaged git diff --check conflict-marker reports before merge commit; _commit_merge_candidate commits without a pathspec.","task_run_checkpoint.py selects _tip_candidate(carrier[\"head_sha\"]) for the commit-only carrier after scoped changes are established.","task_run.py passes candidate_commit[\"sha\"] as target_head only for a committed checkpoint; task_run_completion.py obtains observed_head from scope candidate_carrier and sets payload target_sha from that head.","The supplied failed-lane end-to-end tests exercise unresolved merge, mixed-scope merge, resolved merge SHA propagation, and clean committed-tip propagation against real git repositories.","The checkpoint remains explicitly correctness_verified=false and WIP; state classification still requires abnormal execution and does not confer approval from a candidate SHA."]},{"target":"#878","verdict":"pass","summary":"The Claude backend removes the unsupported top-level $schema before encoding the inline --json-schema argument. For nonzero backend exits, the worker error now includes the first non-empty captured stderr line, and the runtime persists that error in its typed failure receipt while retaining the backend and output lifecycle boundary.","evidence":["reviewer_worker_backend.py loads the schema, pops only the top-level $schema key for claude_p, and serializes the remaining payload into --json-schema.","execute_backend reads and bounds the first non-empty stderr line to 500 characters and appends it to the backend-failed message when the process exits nonzero.","reviewer_worker_runtime.py catches WorkerError and stores str(exc) in the terminal receipt error; reviewer_worker.py serializes that failure receipt and returns nonzero.","Supplied unit tests assert schema-key removal, stderr propagation, unchanged plain errors when stderr is absent or blank, and that a failed backend does not publish pending output.","The runtime still validates normalized output through the canonical schema validator; the patch does not weaken result validation or change backend selection/receipt contracts."]},{"target":"#879","verdict":"pass","summary":"Scope evidence now filters ordinary dotted identifiers and foreign slash tokens using repository top-level names or existing paths, removes the phrase-triggered dotted-token behavior, and retains advisory recall for file-shaped slash tokens such as new files outside known top-level names.","evidence":["task_run_scope_evidence.py has no scope-mismatch substring switch; dotted tokens are considered only when inline code or line-number context makes them candidates, then _keep_candidate applies repository admission.","_keep_candidate accepts candidates under a real top-level name, an existing path, or a file-shaped slash token; this preserves new files under known roots and #880 advisory recall for unknown-root filenames.","The supplied tests cover issue.create/schema identifiers, origin/main, task/x, npm scope and fs/promises rejection; new gateway/scripts file paths; unknown-root zebra/qux.ts recall; and phrase-only dotted-token rejection.","task_run_plan.py continues to record evidence paths as advisory preflight findings; the review did not identify a path from these tokens directly altering declared scope or being treated as proof of ownership."]}],"findings":[],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Merge marker detection depends on git diff --check output spelling and may not establish semantic conflict resolution beyond recognized marker lines.","bin":"bounded residual; no packet evidence of a missed marker form","disposition":"The approach also checks Git's unmerged index and only the marker diagnostics from staged and unstaged diff checks; the tests cover both unstaged conflict and staged marker content. No concrete defect in the reported behavior is established."},{"concern":"Unknown-root tokens ending in a file extension may still be false-positive candidates.","bin":"intentional advisory recall (#880)","disposition":"Retained deliberately by _looks_like_file and covered by the unknown-root new-file test; it is advisory evidence, not an automatic scope expansion."},{"concern":"The inline reviewer-backend tests simulate process outcomes rather than launching an installed Claude CLI.","bin":"evidence limit, not contradiction","disposition":"The issue documents the CLI's behavior and the fix removes the identified unsupported key; the backend command and failure receipt paths are covered. No contrary backend-contract regression appears in the supplied semantic input."}],"next_move":"No blocking follow-up identified for #877, #878, or #879; retain the explicit WIP/unverified checkpoint semantics and #880 advisory recall behavior.","non_claims":["This review did not run the supplied tests or invoke an installed Claude CLI.","The verdict covers only the packet-bound source and test payload; it does not claim broader repository quality or release verification."]}
